    },
    {
      "area": "Authentication",
      "before": "Process-local Express limiter counters, login failure state and OAuth replay Map permitted worker switching and cross-worker replay.",
      "after": "Reuse existing Mongo governance transactions/TTL collection for counters and lockouts; unique majority-acknowledged OAuth claim is atomic across workers. Preserve first-hit-relative windows, denied counts, IP/account identity and configured limits. Mongo outage returns 503; Redis outage does not disable protection."
    },
    {
      "area": "Lifecycle",
      "before": "Six workers lacked stop hooks, and shutdown did not drain all owned work. Expired settings could make shutdown logging throw after storage closed.",
      "after": "Track and stop only started schedules, await active work, clear owned cron registrations, use one idempotent shutdown promise and a 15-second deadline. Leave durable leases intact for uncertain work. Shutdown messages do not depend on settings storage."
    },
    {
      "area": "Cold GitHub persistence",
      "before": "Lazy notification model collection/index creation ran while the GitHub save transaction was open. Actual Mongo trace recorded commit code 112, namespace already in use; retries could exhaust the unchanged 5-second transaction budget.",
      "after": "Await existing notification model initialization before opening the transaction; regression asserts no cold DDL overlaps the first save transaction. This removes the demonstrated notification DDL race, but a later focused run still timed out; complete cold-save reliability is unverified."
    }
